At the beginning of this week I was sitting on a couch reading when
suddenly an idea came from out of the blue and planted itself in my
head.  It was this: You know how that guy showed up recently and
stirred up all this discussion on a sequel to Nethack?  And someone
(can't remember who) said something about it being a bit hard to write
a follow-up to something that ends with being crowned a demigod? 
Well, it's actually quite easy!  Nethack isn't very strong in the plot
department, you know, so all you need for a sequel is a cheap plot
device, like this one:

After you retrieved the Amulet and offered it to <insert deity here>,
lots of good stuff happened to you, like becoming a demigod.  The
Wizard of Yendor still wanted it, though, and stole it off your god,
and now you have to go get it back.  Yes, yes, it's a stupid story, I
know.  I'm working on it.

Okay, so I took the stupid story and decided to make a game with it
(done with Game Maker, nothing special).  It's a platformer, because I
think if it were like real NetHack there wouldn't be much point in
making it.  It's not meant to be an actual sequel, just a tribute. 
I'm thinking of calling it Non-NetHack, since it's going to be
developed by one person and not over the net.  Graphics will be in the
style of those pictures I drew.

Now...I need ideas, especially ones relating to the story, since I've
already got a pretty good idea of what the gameplay will be like. 
Suggestions regarding *anything* will be welcome, though.  Do you
think I should have music?  If yes, someone else will have to do the
music since I'm no good with midi.  One thing I have to get straight,
though: this is not something to get excited over.  Non-NetHack is
still in its very preliminary stages and has a pretty good chance of
becoming vapourware, especially now that I'm suffering a major
motivational crisis.  After lovingly creating 32x32 pixel sprites of
sword-toting @s and tooth-gnashing :s, I realised that yeah, I
probably *should* make them a bit bigger if I want the game window to
be larger than, say, a credit card.  If I can get over the sprite
thing before the end of the holidays, though, then I think the game's
safe.

Any comments?  Anything at all?

